#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
================================================================================
  ISI v5.6 LIVE TRADING STRATEGY  —  OpenAlgo
================================================================================
  Python port of the openalgo-chart TypeScript ISI engine:
    src/utils/indicators/intradaySignalsIndia.ts   (signal detection)
    src/services/backtest/isiBacktestEngine.ts      (sizing, trailing SL, charges wiring)
    src/services/backtest/backtestCharges.ts        (Indian intraday charges model)
    src/services/live/isiLiveTrader.ts              (order placement / management / persistence)

  Runs as an OpenAlgo hosted /python strategy (or standalone). Once started it
  is a server-side process: closing any browser/chart window has no effect on
  it — only stopping it via the OpenAlgo /python UI (or SIGTERM) does.

  Flow per 5-minute candle close (matches isiLiveTrader.ts tickBody exactly):
    1. No position -> run the ISI signal engine on closed candles; if a fresh
       signal is active and passes filters/confirmation/sizing/margin caps,
       place a MARKET entry + broker-side SL-M order.
    2. Position active -> confirm SL order state at the broker, check target,
       compute trailing SL, modify the SL order if it moved.
    3. At EXIT_TIME -> cancel SL + flatten at market, retried until confirmed flat.

  State survives a restart: positions + day counters are written to a JSON
  state file after every entry/trail/exit, and on startup are reconciled
  against the broker's positionbook/orderbook (adopts real broker positions,
  records offline fills, refuses to start if an unrecognized MIS position
  exists it cannot account for) — same contract as isiLiveTrader.ts's
  restoreAndReconcile().

  Usage:
      python isi_v56_live_strategy.py

  No dry-run mode: OpenAlgo's own analyzer/sandbox mode (toggle it in the
  OpenAlgo UI before uploading) is the intended way to test this — orders are
  placed for real through the API either way, and the analyzer decides
  server-side whether they're paper-filled or sent to the broker. That keeps
  this script's order-verification logic (fill checks, SL confirmation,
  retries) identical in test and live runs instead of diverging in a
  DRY_RUN branch that never gets exercised for real.

  OpenAlgo /python host: upload, set parameters, schedule 09:15-15:30.
  Env vars OPENALGO_API_KEY / HOST_SERVER / WEBSOCKET_URL / STRATEGY_ID are
  read automatically when hosted.
================================================================================
"""

